Here's a simple guide and C# sample for migrating users to Azure AD B2C in a .NET 8 application. The process involves exporting user data, preparing it for import, and leveraging Microsoft Graph API or custom policies to migrate users.

Steps for Migrating Users to Azure AD B2C

1. Set Up Azure AD B2C

Create an Azure AD B2C Tenant:

Go to the Azure portal.

Search for "Azure AD B2C" and create a new tenant.

Link it to your Azure subscription.


Register an Application:

Register a web application in Azure AD B2C.

Configure API permissions (Microsoft Graph - User.ReadWrite.All).

Note down the Client ID, Tenant ID, and Client Secret.


Create a User Flow (Sign-up/Sign-in):

Configure user attributes like email, display name, etc.




---

2. Export Existing Users

Export users from your current identity system to a CSV/JSON file.



---

3. Create Migration API or Use Graph API

Use Microsoft Graph to import users in bulk or individually.



---

C# Sample - Migrating Users to Azure AD B2C

Install Required Packages

dotnet add package Microsoft.Graph
dotnet add package Azure.Identity


---

C# Code (User Migration using Microsoft Graph)

using Azure.Identity;
using Microsoft.Graph;
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        var tenantId = "YOUR_TENANT_ID";
        var clientId = "YOUR_CLIENT_ID";
        var clientSecret = "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET";
        var authority = $"https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenantId}";

        var clientSecretCredential = new ClientSecretCredential(tenantId, clientId, clientSecret);
        var graphClient = new GraphServiceClient(clientSecretCredential);

        var users = new List<User>
        {
            new User
            {
                AccountEnabled = true,
                DisplayName = "John Doe",
                MailNickname = "johndoe",
                UserPrincipalName = "johndoe@YOUR_TENANT.onmicrosoft.com",
                PasswordProfile = new PasswordProfile
                {
                    ForceChangePasswordNextSignIn = false,
                    Password = "P@ssword123!"
                }
            }
        };

        foreach (var user in users)
        {
            try
            {
                await graphClient.Users
                    .Request()
                    .AddAsync(user);
                Console.WriteLine($"User {user.DisplayName} created successfully.");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error creating user {user.DisplayName}: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}


---

Explanation of Key Components

GraphServiceClient: Connects to Microsoft Graph.

ClientSecretCredential: Authenticates the app with Azure AD.

User Object: Represents the user being created.

PasswordProfile: Sets an initial password.



---

Testing the Migration

1. Run the application in Visual Studio Code or Visual Studio.


2. Check Azure AD B2C to verify the users have been added.




